================================================================================
MODIFICATIONS
================================================================================

Every project gains an SD-route version next to its baseline: NAVSIM's 4-way driving_command
is removed and a standard-definition route (a 120-point ego-frame polyline built by sdroute/)
is the only navigation signal. The route switch is off by default, so each project's
baseline path is the upstream model. Configs are named <model>_{baseline,sdroute}_agent.

Added to navsim, DrivoR, DiffusionDrive and SafeDrive (identical in all four):
  navsim/agents/sdroute/__init__.py
  navsim/agents/sdroute/route_attention.py    route tokens + gated cross-attention
  navsim/agents/sdroute/route_target.py       loads sdroute/ and builds the route tensor

