models/SafeDrive
  Its baseline is the paper's phase-3 model made camera-only and extended to detect pedestrians
  (safedrive_baseline_agent). The paper's camera + LiDAR model stays trainable and evaluable, and a
  camera-only vehicle variant is added. Only phase-3 checkpoints are released.
  Added
    safedrive_baseline_agent.yaml, safedrive_sdroute_agent.yaml, and the *_CamOnly(_Ped)(_SDRoute)
    phase configs they build on; train_safedrive.sh, cache_safedrive.sh, eval_safedrive.sh,
    cache_metric_safedrive.sh (replacing upstream's train.sh, cache.sh, test.sh);
    planning/script/run_sdroute_backfill.py; agents/safedrive/inference_compat.py;
    .odyssey-safedrive-patch.json (the record that Odyssey's scripts/apply_safedrive_patch.py writes
    after applying its patch; SafeDrive itself does not read it).
  Modified
    SD-route input: modules/decoder_motion.py, modules/transformer_motion.py,
      safedrive_{model,features,config}.py (route cross-attention in both plan decoders; off by
      default).
    Camera-only (use_lidar): safedrive_{config,backbone,features,model,agent}.py,
      modules/transformer_encoder.py, planning/script/run_training.py.
    Pedestrian detection (det_pedestrian): safedrive_{config,model,loss,callback}.py.
    Infrastructure: images cached as uint8 or as paths (safedrive_features.py,
      abstract_agent.py, run_training.py); vectorised detection targets, denoising prep and
      per-camera attention (safedrive_loss.py, safedrive_model.py,
      modules/spatial_cross_attention.py -- same math; CUDA index_add sums cameras in no fixed
      order); only the three cameras read are loaded (safedrive_agent.py); BEV argmax kept on
      CPU during validation (planning/training/agent_lightning_module.py); optional
      save-before-validation checkpoint (run_training.py); top-k query writes through a padded
      scatter and BEV point sampling under a TF32-off context manager (safedrive_model.py,
      modules/encoder.py, helpers in inference_compat.py); `from __future__ import annotations`
      in several modules; no default backbone weights path (upstream's pointed into a home
      directory) and a clear error when timm cannot fetch them (safedrive_{config,backbone}.py).
    Phase2/Phase3 yamls, README.md, docs/install.md, docs/train_eval.md, requirements.txt,
      .gitignore: comments, release instructions, mmdet/spconv pins; README images load from
      upstream at the commit above; .gitignore drops upstream's local helper entries and keeps
      eval_safedrive.sh tracked.
  Removed: make_anchors.sh (the anchors ship), docs/preprocess.md (folded into
    docs/train_eval.md), figure/*.png, safedrive_visualize.py, scripts/evaluation/run_metric_caching.sh.

