models/recogdrive (ReCogDrive)
  Its SD-route version enters differently: the route becomes one token added to the planner's
  ego-status conditioning, and the VLM prompt's navigation line is written from the route as
  text; only a route too short to describe (~0.1% of navtrain) falls back to the command.
  Added
    agents/recogdrive/sdroute_encoder.py (see above), agents/recogdrive/route_text.py;
    recogdrive_sdroute_agent.yaml; scripts/sdroute/*.
  Modified
    SD-route input: agents/recogdrive/recogdrive_{agent,diffusion_planner,features,backbone}.py,
      planning/script/run_training_recogdrive{,_rl}.py, run_recogdrive_accelerate.py,
      planning/training/{agent_lightning_module,dataset}.py.
    Fixes: run_pdm_score_recogdrive.py trims each rank's gathered score bytes to that rank's own
      length (rank 0's length was applied to every rank) and passes the Scene when the agent
      needs it; the planner casts its inputs to the parameter dtype (bf16 under DeepSpeed);
      initialize() fails on a mismatched checkpoint instead of skipping tensors; the "unknown"
      driving command (one-hot slot 3) reads "unknown" in the VLM prompt instead of raising
      IndexError.
    Infrastructure: checkpoint and wandb settings in config/training/default_training.yaml;
      run_training_recogdrive.py calls agent.initialize(), so imitation learning also loads
      agent.checkpoint_path; PDM_DIST_BACKEND=gloo for ranks sharing a GPU
      (run_pdm_score_recogdrive.py, run_training_recogdrive_rl.py); TQDM progress bar;
      torch.load(weights_only=False) for torch >= 2.6; hidden-state caching under no_grad;
      optional bf16 hidden-state cache; LiDAR loading turned off (never read).
    recogdrive_baseline_agent.yaml: upstream recogdrive_agent.yaml, renamed, with the SD-route
      keys added (all off); scripts/**: agent=recogdrive_baseline_agent.
  Removed: committed __pycache__/*.pyc files, assets/.DS_Store, .gitattributes (Git LFS rules)
    and assets/images/framework.jpg (an unreferenced LFS pointer; the README uses framework.png).
